(2561794, 353348, 25678, '<td valign="top">Haha!  We''re you the one asking about how to get a snail to come out of its shell?  Well, if you are, looks like you got it.<br/> <br/>Bonus point for making me laugh!</td>', 'Haha!  We''re you the one asking about how to get a snail to come out of its shell?  Well, if you are, looks like you got it. Bonus point for making me laugh!', '2006-06-28 12:03:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2562100, 353083, 40819, '<td valign="top">I just can''t figure this out. Maybe you can help and I''ll change this post. The guy on the board is so sharp which is great, but the water is too, as whitnessed by the droplets in the air. I could be wrong. The background looks like the blur came from DOF in a long lens. So my point is there really isn''t any "motion blur" in this image, so how do I rate it? <br/>If I rated it just as an image, it would be around a 5. It doesn''t have any pop to me. If it was cropped with just the two sail boarders it would be much higher like an 8. I know you were trying to crop it with the trails of the two boards but I don''t think you needed that to convey the motion. Really good sharp shot of the guy in front too, I know that was not a mistake but a really great shot.<br/> <br/>I am serious if anything I wrote was not appreciated I will remove it before the end of the voting. I only commented because I know how hard you worked on this and wanted just to chime in with some constructive ideas. Be well.<br/> <br/>Mike</td>', 'I just can''t figure this out. Maybe you can help and I''ll change this post. The guy on the board is so sharp which is great, but the water is too, as whitnessed by the droplets in the air. I could be wrong. The background looks like the blur came from DOF in a long lens. So my point is there really isn''t any "motion blur" in this image, so how do I rate it? If I rated it just as an image, it would be around a 5. It doesn''t have any pop to me. If it was cropped with just the two sail boarders it would be much higher like an 8. I know you were trying to crop it with the trails of the two boards but I don''t think you needed that to convey the motion. Really good sharp shot of the guy in front too, I know that was not a mistake but a really great shot. I am serious if anything I wrote was not appreciated I will remove it before the end of the voting. I only commented because I know how hard you worked on this and wanted just to chime in with some constructive ideas. Be well. Mike', '2006-06-28 13:17:55.000000', NULL, 1),
