(2564298, 353379, 38072, '<td valign="top">Nice shot!  I like the background blur from the upwards panning angle.  It would have been great to get the bike and ride more crisp.  I know, though, that there are some limitations in place from the indoor lighting.<br/> <br/>Overall I really like this shot.  I would have given an extra point for a sharper subject.</td>', 'Nice shot!  I like the background blur from the upwards panning angle.  It would have been great to get the bike and ride more crisp.  I know, though, that there are some limitations in place from the indoor lighting. Overall I really like this shot.  I would have given an extra point for a sharper subject.', '2006-06-28 23:25:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564332, 353743, 38072, '<td valign="top">Nice motion in the background.  I can''t tell if you softened the horse in post processing -- I''ve found that my preference in nearly all of these blur shots has been for a sharp subject.  I like the look on the horse''s face, and the main in the air.  Overall, I really like the shot.  I would have given an extra point for a sharper subject.</td>', 'Nice motion in the background.  I can''t tell if you softened the horse in post processing -- I''ve found that my preference in nearly all of these blur shots has been for a sharp subject.  I like the look on the horse''s face, and the main in the air.  Overall, I really like the shot.  I would have given an extra point for a sharper subject.', '2006-06-28 23:30:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564341, 353367, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:32:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564342, 352782, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:32:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564345, 353754, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:32:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564353, 353306, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  It happens less on your shot than many of the others -- I think because there is plenty of contrast between the girl and the background, and the blur on the girl is not overdone.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  It happens less on your shot than many of the others -- I think because there is plenty of contrast between the girl and the background, and the blur on the girl is not overdone.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:34:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564358, 352983, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:34:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564365, 353592, 38072, '<td valign="top">This seems like a good setup, and nice lighting.  I almost missed the blur though.  It would have been nice to have the motion a little more visible.</td>', 'This seems like a good setup, and nice lighting.  I almost missed the blur though.  It would have been nice to have the motion a little more visible.', '2006-06-28 23:37:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564372, 353054, 38072, '<td valign="top">I like the concept here -- and the lighting is good dramatic.  I had a bit of difficulty figuring out what it was.  I think it would have helped me to have a little more light on the Sax so I could see more than just the highlighted reflections.  I generally don''t care much for pictures where I can''t tell what I''m looking at -- and that was my first impression with this shot.  I had to study it to get it.</td>', 'I like the concept here -- and the lighting is good dramatic.  I had a bit of difficulty figuring out what it was.  I think it would have helped me to have a little more light on the Sax so I could see more than just the highlighted reflections.  I generally don''t care much for pictures where I can''t tell what I''m looking at -- and that was my first impression with this shot.  I had to study it to get it.', '2006-06-28 23:39:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564381, 353663, 38072, '<td valign="top">It''s hard for me to see the blur in this shot.  I think if the chick were lit a bit better for the walk it would be more obvious.  With my LCD monitor at work, I didn''t see the blur at all.</td>', 'It''s hard for me to see the blur in this shot.  I think if the chick were lit a bit better for the walk it would be more obvious.  With my LCD monitor at work, I didn''t see the blur at all.', '2006-06-28 23:41:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564384, 353625, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''m missing the blur here?</td>', 'I''m missing the blur here?', '2006-06-28 23:42:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564390, 353464, 38072, '<td valign="top">I think we''re missing a lot, because of the blown half of the picture.  It looks like it might be a pretty fantastic shot if the brightness were cut back so we coud see some of the details of the fireworks.</td>', 'I think we''re missing a lot, because of the blown half of the picture.  It looks like it might be a pretty fantastic shot if the brightness were cut back so we coud see some of the details of the fireworks.', '2006-06-28 23:43:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564399, 353214, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''m missing the motion here...  It looks like the lights behind the truck are being moved...  And that''s certainly motion blur -- but it doesn''t impart any sense of motion in the subject.  I think I would better like a shot similar to this where the truck was actually rolling (the wheels would blur) past a blurred background that was caused by the movement of the truck.  Perhaps it''s just a difference in "artistic preference" though.</td>', 'I''m missing the motion here...  It looks like the lights behind the truck are being moved...  And that''s certainly motion blur -- but it doesn''t impart any sense of motion in the subject.  I think I would better like a shot similar to this where the truck was actually rolling (the wheels would blur) past a blurred background that was caused by the movement of the truck.  Perhaps it''s just a difference in "artistic preference" though.', '2006-06-28 23:47:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564407, 353348, 38072, '<td valign="top">Wow...  I''m confused with this picture!  <br/>What''s the motorcycle resting on?  It looks like it''s floating in air.<br/>A snail?!<br/>The background is blurred, but I think it''s just out of focus.<br/>There''s some blur in the front wheel, because it''s spinning, but the back wheel isn''t.<br/>Is this bike moving or not?<br/> <br/>It''s a cute idea -- I like the idea.  Perhaps if you''d managed to get both wheels spinning and get a little motion in the background this would have been a more clever shot.</td>', 'Wow...  I''m confused with this picture!  What''s the motorcycle resting on?  It looks like it''s floating in air.A snail?!The background is blurred, but I think it''s just out of focus.There''s some blur in the front wheel, because it''s spinning, but the back wheel isn''t.Is this bike moving or not? It''s a cute idea -- I like the idea.  Perhaps if you''d managed to get both wheels spinning and get a little motion in the background this would have been a more clever shot.', '2006-06-28 23:49:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564413, 353351, 38072, '<td valign="top">The image isn''t crisp -- I can''t tell if that''s because of motion or just poor focus.  I do see some motion in the prop, but I really have to look to find that.</td>', 'The image isn''t crisp -- I can''t tell if that''s because of motion or just poor focus.  I do see some motion in the prop, but I really have to look to find that.', '2006-06-28 23:50:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564416, 353423, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  That really happens on this shot.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  That really happens on this shot.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:51:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564418, 353468, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  I also don''t prefer pictures that I can''t tell what I''m looking at.  At first glance, that''s definitely true in this shot (for me at least).  Reading the title helps, but then I''m wondering where the TV is.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  I also don''t prefer pictures that I can''t tell what I''m looking at.  At first glance, that''s definitely true in this shot (for me at least).  Reading the title helps, but then I''m wondering where the TV is.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:52:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564421, 353720, 38072, '<td valign="top">This is an interesting shot.  I can''t really tell what I''m looking at behind the vase.  I don''t see movement in the vase, and I can''t tell what''s behind.  What is that?</td>', 'This is an interesting shot.  I can''t really tell what I''m looking at behind the vase.  I don''t see movement in the vase, and I can''t tell what''s behind.  What is that?', '2006-06-28 23:53:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564423, 350223, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.', '2006-06-28 23:53:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564434, 353198, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  I also don''t tend to be attracted to shots where I can''t tell what I''m seeing.  I find myself trying to figure out what this is (and being frustrated when I can''t) rather than appreciating it as abstract art.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  I also don''t tend to be attracted to shots where I can''t tell what I''m seeing.  I find myself trying to figure out what this is (and being frustrated when I can''t) rather than appreciating it as abstract art.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:55:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564436, 353740, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  I also don''t tend to be attracted to shots where I can''t tell what I''m seeing.  I find myself trying to figure out what this is (and being frustrated when I can''t) rather than appreciating it as abstract art.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  I also don''t tend to be attracted to shots where I can''t tell what I''m seeing.  I find myself trying to figure out what this is (and being frustrated when I can''t) rather than appreciating it as abstract art.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:55:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564438, 353708, 38072, '<td valign="top">I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  I also don''t tend to be attracted to shots where I can''t tell what I''m seeing.  I find myself trying to figure out what this is (and being frustrated when I can''t) rather than appreciating it as abstract art.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.</td>', 'I''ve given the same basic comment on quite a few shots -- my preference (as I discovered while looking at a number of these blur shots) is for a sharp subject.  When there is no sharp subject, my eye wanders around trying to find something to focus on.  I also don''t tend to be attracted to shots where I can''t tell what I''m seeing.  I find myself trying to figure out what this is (and being frustrated when I can''t) rather than appreciating it as abstract art.  Perhaps just a difference in artistic preference.', '2006-06-28 23:55:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(2564446, 353714, 38072, '<td valign="top">I definitely see motion here, but I''m not seeing the motion blur.</td>', 'I definitely see motion here, but I''m not seeing the motion blur.', '2006-06-28 23:56:38.000000', NULL, 1),
