(2578710, 352512, 42135, '<td valign="top">Congrats!!!  It is a beautiful shot!!</td>', 'Congrats!!!  It is a beautiful shot!!', '2006-07-03 11:59:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(2578713, 353515, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by glad2badad:</b></div><hr/><i> This almost looks like a toy setup.  At first, from the thumbnail, I thought it was.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>That''s what I thought at first too ... there was a recent thread about a genre of photos where you take a real object/scene and try to make it look as though it was shot with models/props -- this photo is a pretty good example. Nice work!</td>', 'Originally posted by glad2badad: This almost looks like a toy setup.  At first, from the thumbnail, I thought it was. That''s what I thought at first too ... there was a recent thread about a genre of photos where you take a real object/scene and try to make it look as though it was shot with models/props -- this photo is a pretty good example. Nice work!', '2006-07-03 12:00:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(2578740, 353119, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by karmabreeze:</b></div><hr/><i> I like it as an abstract, but it would benefit from a sweep through Neat Image to eliminate much of the noise artifacts. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>I feel much the same, though I don''t think I noticed the noise as much the first time I looked at it.</td>', 'Originally posted by karmabreeze: I like it as an abstract, but it would benefit from a sweep through Neat Image to eliminate much of the noise artifacts.  I feel much the same, though I don''t think I noticed the noise as much the first time I looked at it.', '2006-07-03 12:05:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(2578763, 352883, 1031, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by karmabreeze:</b></div><hr/><i> Interesting idea. The door frame(?) at the left side is distracting, leave the composition looking unbalances. </i></td></tr></table> <br/>Yeah, that''s the streetlight pole the pinwheels are mounted on. The shot with the "best" blur(?) had that angle -- the ones which missed the pole were either too blurry, not blurry enough, or had some other problem ...</td>', 'Originally posted by karmabreeze: Interesting idea. The door frame(?) at the left side is distracting, leave the composition looking unbalances.  Yeah, that''s the streetlight pole the pinwheels are mounted on. The shot with the "best" blur(?) had that angle -- the ones which missed the pole were either too blurry, not blurry enough, or had some other problem ...', '2006-07-03 12:09:51.000000', NULL, 0),
