(2579676, 353708, 19831, '<td valign="top">This is a very nice abstract. A nice, soothing soft feel. Great colors, I like the touch of green with the red, adds much to the shot, IMO. Composed well, and good lighting, there is enough shadows/dark areas to add to the nice flow of the image. There is a nice corner to corner travel across the image. Nicely done. <br/> <br/>Yes, Neil is the abstract master, isn''t he? :-) I find him very inspiring and a good critic of the genre. I too wish there were more people that liked a good abstract, I love ''em! I''ve submitted a few, only one that did well at all was ''Saturday'', in the last ''Abstract'' challenge. I always get amused by the "I can''t tell what it is" comments. :-) I mean, c''mon, it''s obviously an abstract, you don''t have to know what it is...<br/> <br/>Anyways, nice job on this one. Anyone that does appriciate a good abstract I''m sure will like it!</td>', 'This is a very nice abstract. A nice, soothing soft feel. Great colors, I like the touch of green with the red, adds much to the shot, IMO. Composed well, and good lighting, there is enough shadows/dark areas to add to the nice flow of the image. There is a nice corner to corner travel across the image. Nicely done.  Yes, Neil is the abstract master, isn''t he? :-) I find him very inspiring and a good critic of the genre. I too wish there were more people that liked a good abstract, I love ''em! I''ve submitted a few, only one that did well at all was ''Saturday'', in the last ''Abstract'' challenge. I always get amused by the "I can''t tell what it is" comments. :-) I mean, c''mon, it''s obviously an abstract, you don''t have to know what it is... Anyways, nice job on this one. Anyone that does appriciate a good abstract I''m sure will like it!', '2006-07-03 16:12:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(2579700, 352846, 58125, '<td valign="top">Wow! Facial expression, color, angles and the winner. Did you take great photos and enjoy the race? Thank you for sharing.</td>', 'Wow! Facial expression, color, angles and the winner. Did you take great photos and enjoy the race? Thank you for sharing.', '2006-07-03 16:18:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(2579705, 353708, 8891, '<td valign="top">Finished right ahead of you with a similar idea. Thought it was enhanced but got comments like racing flowers and Really fast flowers! Nice colors? I think this is a lot more effective than mine as the camera pan gives the image a painterly effect without a filter. Great stuff! Going to try it again? I am.</td>', 'Finished right ahead of you with a similar idea. Thought it was enhanced but got comments like racing flowers and Really fast flowers! Nice colors? I think this is a lot more effective than mine as the camera pan gives the image a painterly effect without a filter. Great stuff! Going to try it again? I am.', '2006-07-03 16:19:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2579709, 352736, 41337, '<td valign="top">That is pretty cool. I bet if something in the shot (a ball perhaps?) was visible and was somewhat in focus it would have scored much higher. The colors in it is probably what scored it over 6. Regardless, it''s a great looking abstract.</td>', 'That is pretty cool. I bet if something in the shot (a ball perhaps?) was visible and was somewhat in focus it would have scored much higher. The colors in it is probably what scored it over 6. Regardless, it''s a great looking abstract.', '2006-07-03 16:20:51.000000', NULL, 0),
(2579741, 353728, 31133, '<td valign="top">Well now, Laurie, I have to apologize for my too hasty comment below. The forum thread about the results of this challenge brought me back for a second look. I apologize for my comment suggesting higher contrast when you actually intended for the contrast to be low.<br/> <br/>Looking at the image a second time, it''s easy for me to understand why you reduced the contrast. The low contrast contributes to the feeling of the bird being one with the water, and the water one with the bird. So I take back the contrast remark :-) Instead I suggest (and maybe just to protect my own dignity, heehee) that a black frame might have kept my eye in this subtle scene a bit longer, instead of just giving you a 5 and moving on. I stand by the positive parts of my comment below, though! Also, I really like the movement in the wing. Nice work and sorry for my looking too quickly during voting.</td>', 'Well now, Laurie, I have to apologize for my too hasty comment below. The forum thread about the results of this challenge brought me back for a second look. I apologize for my comment suggesting higher contrast when you actually intended for the contrast to be low. Looking at the image a second time, it''s easy for me to understand why you reduced the contrast. The low contrast contributes to the feeling of the bird being one with the water, and the water one with the bird. So I take back the contrast remark :-) Instead I suggest (and maybe just to protect my own dignity, heehee) that a black frame might have kept my eye in this subtle scene a bit longer, instead of just giving you a 5 and moving on. I stand by the positive parts of my comment below, though! Also, I really like the movement in the wing. Nice work and sorry for my looking too quickly during voting.', '2006-07-03 16:29:52.000000', NULL, 0),
