(2584012, 353403, 42792, '<td valign="top">Thank you for all the great comments.  I don''t have this technique totally clean yet but the score is better than expected.  So it''s really encouraging.  Most found the left blur of the runner in front distracting but it was part of my composition and hence, the title.  I wished I had been able to capture him more within the frame but he was too fast.  Also, the original was strictly horizontal (as digitalknight suggested) but I found it too flat.  Tested a few tilt angles and found this was best IMO (but maybe not).  Appreciate all the feedback tho'' (yes including yours MPRPRO). :)</td>', 'Thank you for all the great comments.  I don''t have this technique totally clean yet but the score is better than expected.  So it''s really encouraging.  Most found the left blur of the runner in front distracting but it was part of my composition and hence, the title.  I wished I had been able to capture him more within the frame but he was too fast.  Also, the original was strictly horizontal (as digitalknight suggested) but I found it too flat.  Tested a few tilt angles and found this was best IMO (but maybe not).  Appreciate all the feedback tho'' (yes including yours MPRPRO). :)', '2006-07-04 13:55:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(2584591, 353383, 41337, '<td valign="top">Holy crap. Yeah I would say you were robbed. 5.0? Now I feel like an outcast giving out one of those lonely 9+ scores. That''s got to be the highest score I''ve ever given to an image that finished this low. People just don''t understand.</td>', 'Holy crap. Yeah I would say you were robbed. 5.0? Now I feel like an outcast giving out one of those lonely 9+ scores. That''s got to be the highest score I''ve ever given to an image that finished this low. People just don''t understand.', '2006-07-04 17:11:13.000000', NULL, 0),
