(2595509, 352358, 47933, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club Cory!<br/> <br/>This is a difficult image for me to critique as there is not much I''d change here. Personally I feel that it would''ve even done better if the voters were more open minded that zoom blur is truly considered motion blur. Heck, it even says so in the challenge description. I like the emotion on the singers face and the upright bass player behind her is a nice touch.<br/> <br/>As I said, there is not much I''d change for this exact shot so I''ll comment, for future challenge reference, as to what might''ve got you a better score. Voters here really dig the color - the more the better. They need that "pop" to make them hand out high scores. If this jazz bar had some colorful neon lights behind the singer I think you would''ve done better. This would''ve added the "pop" I mentioned, plus neon lights with zoom blur are most interesting indeed. <br/> <br/>Overall, an excellent shot that should''ve placed much higher in my honest opinion.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the opportunity to critique this image Cory.<br/> <br/>Cheers - Phil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club Cory! This is a difficult image for me to critique as there is not much I''d change here. Personally I feel that it would''ve even done better if the voters were more open minded that zoom blur is truly considered motion blur. Heck, it even says so in the challenge description. I like the emotion on the singers face and the upright bass player behind her is a nice touch. As I said, there is not much I''d change for this exact shot so I''ll comment, for future challenge reference, as to what might''ve got you a better score. Voters here really dig the color - the more the better. They need that "pop" to make them hand out high scores. If this jazz bar had some colorful neon lights behind the singer I think you would''ve done better. This would''ve added the "pop" I mentioned, plus neon lights with zoom blur are most interesting indeed.  Overall, an excellent shot that should''ve placed much higher in my honest opinion. Thanks for the opportunity to critique this image Cory. Cheers - Phil', '2006-07-07 00:21:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(2596005, 353218, 19959, '<td valign="top">Hello from the critique club.<br/> <br/>Hi Carl,<br/>This is a very nicely observed photo. You have definately achieved what you set out to. You had a good selction of feedback on this picture and a lot of people appreciated the impressionist/painterly feel. Great work.<br/> <br/>It is a shame that these type of pictures do not tend to score as well as they should, perhaps because voters spend so little time on each image. Your photo is subtle and as such perhaps does not have that attention grabbing quality that would lead to a 6+ score.<br/> <br/>Personally I very much like it, although it somehow manages to give an impression of being cramped which feels odd in a landscape. Perhaps this is the tight crop.<br/> <br/>I wonder also if it could be improved by the inclusion of a static object, such as a gate, rock, tree or person to ''anchor'' the picture.<br/> <br/>Overall an excellent take on the challenge (IMO) I would like to try something similar myself so in that way inspirational also. Great work.<br/> <br/>Regards<br/> <br/>Chris<br/></td>', 'Hello from the critique club. Hi Carl,This is a very nicely observed photo. You have definately achieved what you set out to. You had a good selction of feedback on this picture and a lot of people appreciated the impressionist/painterly feel. Great work. It is a shame that these type of pictures do not tend to score as well as they should, perhaps because voters spend so little time on each image. Your photo is subtle and as such perhaps does not have that attention grabbing quality that would lead to a 6+ score. Personally I very much like it, although it somehow manages to give an impression of being cramped which feels odd in a landscape. Perhaps this is the tight crop. I wonder also if it could be improved by the inclusion of a static object, such as a gate, rock, tree or person to ''anchor'' the picture. Overall an excellent take on the challenge (IMO) I would like to try something similar myself so in that way inspirational also. Great work. Regards Chris', '2006-07-07 04:30:24.000000', NULL, 0),
